# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Operator notes for a specific machine, kept out of the repository by design:
# everything needed to reproduce a result belongs in README.md instead.
run.txt

# Generated data (reproducible via scripts/prepare_datasets.py)
data/raw/
data/BZR_MD.json
data/Cuneiform.json
data/*_bond.json
# data/pdb_contact.json is deliberately NOT ignored. See scripts/prepare_datasets.py:
# it is the one collection this repository cannot rebuild, so the built file IS the
# source and it has to travel with the code.

# Experiment outputs. The summary artefacts are tracked: every number the
# study reports lives in one of them, and a claim whose evidence is
# not in the repository cannot be checked by anyone who clones it.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-24. This rule used to exclude every per-seed run, on the
# stated grounds that they are "twenty times the size of everything else
# combined". Measured, the seven excluded files come to 384K against a 10M
# repository -- about four percent, not twenty times. The reason was wrong, and
# by the time it was checked the rule was blocking exactly what the paragraph
# above demands: a table in the manuscript was generated from those files and
# could not be reproduced from a clone. Restricting to the tracked half gave 11
# cells instead of 61 and a different worst case. They are tracked now.
# Pre-audit outputs. Every number in these came from code with two defects since
# fixed -- the fitness anchored on the search bound, and the reported best ignoring
# the support threshold -- so they were deleted. They are ignored rather than merely
# deleted because a machine that still holds untracked copies re-adds all twelve the
# moment someone runs `git add results`, which is exactly how they came back once.
results/budget_regimes_*.csv
# results/pareto_*.csv used to exclude per-seed output from run_pareto.py, which was
# deleted with the rest of the retired runner generation. The glob outlived it and
# silently swallowed pareto_size_*.csv -- a 63-row summary from a 6.2 hour run --
# so the artefact never reached the repository and nothing said so. Excluding by
# name goes stale at exactly the moment something new is added.
results/pareto_comparison_*.csv
results/diversity_*.csv
results/timing_*.csv
results/size_BZR_MD.csv
results/size_Cuneiform.csv
# Unsuffixed degeneracy names: no run can write these any more (--suffix is required),
# so anything appearing under them is a stale copy from before that change.
results/degeneracy_frontier.csv
results/degeneracy_gamma.csv
results/figures/
results/logs/

# The manuscript, its sources and the papers read for it now live in ../paper/, a sibling
# of this checkout rather than a filtered subdirectory of it. Nothing here needs excluding
# from a push any more, which is the point: the cheapest gate is the one that does not
# have to exist.


# Output of the small end-to-end run in README.md; a check, not an artefact.
results/*_smoke.*
